meta-cubie-a7s
==============

Yocto (scarthgap) BSP layer for the Radxa Cubie A7S (Allwinner A733).

Kernel, U-Boot, ARISC/SCP firmware, onboard wifi/bt (AIC8800D80 over USB)
and SD card layout. Builds from Radxa's own sources, pinned. The closed binaries
the board needs (BL31, DRAM init, SCP, wifi firmware, GPU, NPU and video libraries)
are downloaded by the build, never stored here; the top-level README lists each one
with its maker and where it comes from.

Unofficial community project, not made, endorsed or supported by Radxa,
Allwinner, Imagination Technologies, VeriSilicon, the Yocto Project or any
other company or project whose software it builds.


Dependencies
------------

Required:

  URI: https://git.yoctoproject.org/poky
  branch: scarthgap
  layers: meta

Optional, adds the header tools (gpiod tools, Python gpiod/periphery/smbus2/spidev,
dynamic-layers/openembedded-layer):

  URI: https://git.openembedded.org/meta-openembedded
  branch: scarthgap
  layers: meta-oe, plus meta-python for the Python libraries

Build host: x86_64 only (the SCP firmware uses Radxa's prebuilt RISC-V toolchain).

The images, the QB OS distro, ROS 2 and ONNX Runtime live in meta-cubie-robot,
which sits on top of this layer.


Using it
--------

Set MACHINE = "cubie-a7s". The board's drivers, firmware and userspace (wifi,
NPU, video engines, GPU, cooling, header tools) are in MACHINE_EXTRA_RRECOMMENDS,
pull them into your image (packagegroup-base does, core-image-minimal doesn't).

gst-omx (hardware video) is flagged commercial, your distro or local.conf needs
LICENSE_FLAGS_ACCEPTED += "commercial_gstreamer1.0-omx" to build it.

Options, in local.conf or site.conf:

  CUBIE_WIFI_COUNTRY  wifi country, ISO code like "IT" (default "00", the world rules)
  CUBIE_COOLING       "passive" (default, bare board or heatsink) or "fan"
  CUBIE_HEADER        header functions merged into the device tree at build time,
                      e.g. "pwm1-1 twi2 uart2" (default: none, every pin is a GPIO)

The top-level README of the repo has the details and the list of header functions.

Write the .wic from tmp/deploy/images/cubie-a7s/ to an SD card:

  sudo dd if=<image>.wic of=/dev/mmcblkX bs=4M status=progress conv=fsync

Serial console is on the 30 pin header (pin 8 TX, pin 10 RX, pin 6 GND),
115200 8N1, shows up as ttyAS0 on the board.


Wifi
----

The meta-cubie-robot images connect at boot from WIFI_SSID/WIFI_PSK. By hand:

  ip link set wlan0 up
  wpa_passphrase "SSID" "password" > /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf
  wpa_supplicant -B -i wlan0 -c /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf -D nl80211
  udhcpc -i wlan0

Only run one wpa_supplicant, a second one makes association fail
("Match already configured").


